The sticky retention feature can fail to protect a watched child-phase-0 mapping that is already the current best at the start of a recovery phase. This is a functional gap in the new policy.

Review comment:

- [P2] Seed sticky state from the existing best cut — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:5542-5542
  When area recovery enters `Map_MatchNodePhase` with `pCutBest` already selecting the watched child in phase 0, this initializes the sticky guard as empty, so the first accepted child-missing replacement bypasses `Map_Stmap82MaybeBlockStickyReplacement`. This misses exactly the case where the previous best mapping should be retained unless the replacement exceeds the timing window; initialize the sticky match from `pCutBest`/`MatchBest` when it already has child phase 0.
